ered-serve's zipserv_p4flat_ext \"\n                \"extension to build successfully.\")\n        # Bypass DietGPUKVCompressor.__init__ (it loads DietGPU and allocates\n        # an ANS workspace we don't need); initialise the shared state directly.\n        TensorCompressor.__init__(self, comp_stream=comp_stream)\n        self.comp_stream = comp_stream\n        self.batch_decomp_stream = torch.cuda.Stream(priority=0)\n        # One-stream KV decode: when set, the loader points batch_decomp_stream\n        # at exec_stream so the decode (H2D + kernels + breakdown events) runs on\n        # the compute stream — used as a plain attribute, no per-call resolution.\n        self._kv_decode_on_compute = os.getenv(\n            \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_DECODE_ON_COMPUTE\", \"0\") == \"1\"\n        # KV-load stream separation: run the compressed-blob H2D on the\n        # dedicated load_kv_stream (wired by the loader) instead of\n        # batch_decomp_stream, with a 2-slot blob ring so layer L+1's H2D\n        # pipelines with layer L's decode.  load_kv_stream is gated on\n        # \"QKV weights loaded\" by the graph wrapper, so the blob H2D starts\n        # when the single copy engine is free of weight H2D — otherwise it\n        # queues behind weight and the _kv_h2d_begin.._kv_dec_h2d interval\n        # absorbs that wait (small-batch KVLoad read ~= WLoad).  Decode\n        # kernels stay on batch_decomp_stream (what exec's attn barrier waits\n        # on).  Always on — the blob H2D runs on load_kv_stream whenever the\n        # loader wires one (it aliases it to load_weight_stream), and falls back\n        # to the single-stream fused H2D+decode only when no load_kv_stream is\n        # wired (e.g. a standalone compressor with no loader).\n        self.load_kv_stream = None   # wired by the loader after construction\n        self._dec_blob_ring_idx = 0\n        self._kv_split_h2d_enabled = (\n            os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_KV_NO_SPLIT\", \"0\") != \"1\")\n        # Set by the loader from time_breakdown.  When False, the decode skips\n        # the breakdown-only event records (_kv_h2d_begin) — the per-step CUDA\n        # event record() was ~12% of forward-thread CPU in profiling.\n        self._tb = False\n\n        # Per-decode metadata (slots / valid_rows / exc_cnt / is_raw) H2D.\n        # Default = async ring of pinned buffers, event-gated so a lagging\n        # in-flight H2D is never overwritten on reuse — the exact failure that\n        # forced the old synchronous ``torch.stack(...).cuda()`` (pageable ->\n        # ~1 ms/graph CPU dispatch that starves the GPU).  Set\n        # TIERED_SERVE_KV_META_SYNC=1 to restore that legacy sync path.\n        self._meta_sync_fallback = os.getenv(\n            \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_META_SYNC\", \"0\") == \"1\"\n        self._meta_ring_n = 0\n        self._meta_ring_pi = None   # list[pinned int32 [5*cap]]  (cs,vrk,eck,vrv,ecv)\n        self._meta_ring_pu = None   # list[pinned uint8 [2*cap]]  (is_raw k,v)\n        self._meta_ring_b = None    # list[pinned int64 [cap]]    (block_ids)\n        self._meta_ring_ev = None   # list[cuda.Event] gating buffer reuse\n        self._meta_ring_idx = 0\n\n        # Reused, codec-agnostic persistent-slot bookkeeping (see base class).\n        self._compressed_kv: Dict[int, Any] = {}\n        self._persistent_valid: Dict[int, bytearray] = {}\n        self._kv_slot: Dict[int, torch.Tensor] = {}\n        self._kv_slot_np: Dict[int, Any] = {}   # numpy authority (shared mem)\n        self._kv_slot_block: Dict[int, List[int]] = {}\n        # P4Flat free-list slot management (overrides the base dense\n        # swap-with-last).  ``_kv_active_count`` is repurposed as the staging\n        # HIGH-WATER-MARK (max-assigned-slot + 1 = the [0:hwm] extent the decode\n        # H2D copies); freed slots go to a per-layer min-heap and are refilled\n        # lowest-first so hwm — hence the decode over-copy — stays tight, and\n        # top-of-range frees shrink hwm